course: dictionary
lesson: 1777
title: Cliff and cliffhanger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cliff is a high, steep wall of rock or earth, often at the edge of the sea. «The gulls wheeled above the chalk cliffs.» The words high and steep are clues: a cliff is not a gentle slope.
explain: Cliffs are shaped over time. Waves wear the rock away, so the edge can crumble. «Stay back from the cliff edge.» That is why you keep well away from a cliff top.
explain: Cliffhanger is a different word that uses the same idea. «Ella gasped, «That was a cliffhanger!»» Nobody is hanging off a rock. The story stopped at an exciting moment, so you want to know what happens next. When a word fits oddly, look at the words around it.
fact: A cliff is a high, steep wall of rock or earth, often at the edge of the sea.
fact: Waves wear away rock over many years, and this forms cliffs.
fact: «Chalk cliffs» are cliffs made of chalk.
fact: A cliffhanger is a story or episode that ends at an exciting moment.
fact: Rock wallabies climb cliffs, and peregrine falcons nest on tall buildings like the cliffs they use in the wild.
exercise: «Lemmings do not jump off cliffs on purpose.» What is a cliff? | A flat field of grass with sheep on it | A small stream running down a hill | *A high, steep wall of rock or earth, often at the sea's edge
exercise: «Stay back from the cliff edge, because it can crumble.» Why should you stay back? | Because cliffs are warm and cosy | Because the ground there might be soft and break away | Because the grass there is very tasty | *Because the edge can crumble and fall
exercise: Ella says, «That was a cliffhanger!» What does cliffhanger mean? | A very high rock you can climb | A bird that nests high up | *A story that ends at an exciting moment | A sad, quiet ending
test: «Peregrine falcons nest on tall buildings, like the cliffs they use in the wild.» What kind of place is a cliff here? | A flat road for cars | A small pond full of fish | *A tall, steep place high up | A soft cushion
test: «The episode ended on a cliffhanger, and I can't wait for next week!» What does cliffhanger mean? | A worry about heights | A funny joke | A tall rock by the sea | *A story that stops at an exciting moment
exam: «The waves have worn the rock away, and the chalk cliffs now crumble into the sea.» What are cliffs? | Small pebbles on the beach | Large sandy dunes | *Tall, steep walls of rock at the edge of the sea | Deep caves under the sea
